{title: 121 - Go, Tell It On the Mountain}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #121 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 121}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F/C]Go, tell it on [Dm]the mountain,
[Dm]Over the hills and everywhere:
[F/C]Go, tell it on the [C]mountain
[C]That Jesus [C7/Bb]Christ [Dm/A]is born!
[C]While shepherds kept their [Bb]watching
[Bb]O’er silent [Dm/A]flocks by night,
[F/C]Behold throughout the heavens
[Am]There shone a [Dm/F]holy light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[C]Go, tell it on [F/C]the mountain,
[F]Over the [Gm]hills and everywhere:
[Gm/Bb]Go, tell it on [Dm/A]the mountain
[Dm/A]That Jesus Christ is born!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F/C]The shepherds [Dm]feared and trembled
[F/C]When lo! Above [C]the earth
[Bb]Rang out the angel [Dm/A]chorus
[Am]That hailed our [Dm/F]Savior's birth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F/C]Down in a lowly [Dm]manger
[F/C]The humble Christ [C]was born,
[Bb]And brought us God's [Dm/A]salvation
[Am]That blessed Christmas [Dm/F]morn.
{end_of_verse}
